{"explanation": "No clear, unit-specific signal survives. The strongest original effects were weaker activity for left-facing or left-placed subjects (rows 2, 3, 13, 15). All four failed on new photos, and the left-third effects even reversed, so those effects were likely noise from very small groups (5 to 6 photos). The left-facing effect in row 2 stayed positive (percentile 88) but was not unusual. The remaining hint is that the unit is weaker on black-and-white or nearly colorless photos than on tinted or normal-color ones (rows 24, 26, 27). That rests on only 5 photos, and row 27 is shared with a similar unit. There is also a mild preference for sharp over slightly blurry subjects (row 31, percentile 93). Overall the unit seems to respond weakly to color presence and image sharpness, with no reliable compositional or orientation tuning.", "rows": [26]}
```

